# Operator intakes (local disk)

When filing operator intakes while Cursor runs on the same machine as the swarm:

- Write to `.swarmforge/operator/INTAKE-<slug>.md` only.
- The specifier reads intakes directly from local disk — no git commit or push is needed or useful.
- Do not file operator intakes under `backlog/INTAKE-*.md` for this workflow.
- Do not force-add `.swarmforge/` to git; that path is gitignored by design.
- Match how other intakes work tonight: plain local files, never tracked.

After the specifier drains an intake into `backlog/paused/`, move the source file to `.swarmforge/operator/archive/` (per specifier.prompt).
